Corresponding source
--------------------
The exact source for this package is the Lychee Dev repository at the commit
recorded in release.json, with corresponding source archives attached to the
matching release on GitHub:
https://github.com/Follen/Lychee-Dev/releases/tag/v<version>
The product version is defined only by release/version.json.

Distributed payload
-------------------
native/windows-amd64/lycheedev.exe  native Rust CLI
bin/lycheedev.mjs                  Node launcher (platform/integrity check and
                                   argument, stream and exit-code forwarding)
payload/addon/                     existing Lychee Dev Lua addon
payload/skill/                     first-party Agent Skill
payload/tool/luac/                 pinned managed Lua 5.1 compiler

Rust dependency closure
-----------------------
The Rust dependency closure is appended to this file when the package is
assembled. It lists every reachable Cargo.lock dependency of the native
executable with the exact license text from the crate or from the recorded
license supplement. The supplements are recorded in release/licenses/catalog.json;
the build/package check is tools/rust-license-inventory.mjs.

Two registry crates are consumed as exact local patch sources for the Windows
TLS connector: native-tls 0.2.18 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and schannel 0.1.29 (MIT).
Their original license files are retained under vendor/, and the exact source
identity, archive hashes and replayable delta are recorded in
vendor/tls-name-adaptation.json and vendor/tls-verification-name.patch. The
adaptation separates SNI and certificate-verification names; original
certificate chain/name policy and trust behavior are unchanged.

Lua 5.1.5
---------
The managed Lua 5.1.5 compiler/runtime is built from the official Lua source
(MIT, PUC-Rio) and its notice is appended to this file when the package is
assembled. It is part of the native payload used by Source syntax validation and
Live probe tooling; it is not an npm dependency.

