--------------------------------------
Go-derived Data compatibility code
  The redirect/reference handling, gzip framing, fixed Host/canonical-endpoint
  rules and SOCKS5 handshake adapters under
  crates/lycheedev-data/src/remote/transport/ adapt Go 1.27.1 standard-library
  behavior. They remain Copyright 2009 The Go Authors under BSD-3-Clause; the
  complete notice is retained in
  crates/lycheedev-data/src/remote/transport/GO-LICENSE.
  crates/lycheedev-data/src/hotfix/remote/entities.rs is generated from Go
  1.27.1 HTML entity data and retains the Go notice in
  crates/lycheedev-data/src/hotfix/remote/GO-HTML-LICENSE.
  crates/lycheedev-windows/src/mailbox_input/go_unicode/ contains generated Go
  Unicode 17.0.0 case-folding data under the same BSD-3-Clause notice
  (crates/lycheedev-windows/src/mailbox_input/go_unicode/LICENSE).

Bob Jenkins lookup3 checksum
  The CASC index corruption check uses the public-domain lookup3 hash (May 2006)
  by Bob Jenkins (https://burtleburtle.net/bob/c/lookup3.c). It is not a
  cryptographic integrity primitive and no upstream source file is redistributed.

SQLite
  The workspace uses the bundled SQLite distribution through rusqlite;
  SQLite is dedicated to the public domain by its authors
  (https://sqlite.org/copyright.html). The crate-level license text is included
  in the appended Rust dependency closure.
